            <div xml:id="d397-a3">

                <pb facs="0812" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 3.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the Treasury, to Mr. Thomas,
                        collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">John L. Thomas</hi>, Jr., <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Collector of Customs, Baltimore:</hi></p>
                <p>Department informed that expedition in violation of neutrality-laws is expected
                    to embark from the capes of Virginia; send Northerner down to cruise in that
                    vicinity, watching and detaining suspicious vessels. Expedition consists of
                    three tugs, one named H. McCool, two schooners, and one sloop.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                            Treasury.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
